==English==

===Etymology===
From [[French]], from Old French, from the Old Italian ''cavalcata'' from ''cavalcare'', which meant to ride on horseback, from Medieval Latin ''caballicāre'', from the [[Latin]] ''[[caballus]]'', which means [[horse]].

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/ˈkævəlˌkeɪd/ or /ˌkævəlˈkeɪd/}}
*{{audio|en-us-cavalcade.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*:Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-eɪd|-eɪd]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[company]] of [[rider]]s.
# A [[parade]].
# A [[trail ride]], usually more than one day long

====Synonyms====
*{{italbrac|company of riders}}: [[company]]
*{{italbrac|parade}}: [[parade]], [[procession]]

